[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     74[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     75[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     76[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `PNGAPI`, `PNGCBAPI`, `PNG_EMPTY`, `PNG_ALLOCATED`, `PNG_DEPRECATED`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     77[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `PNG_PRIVATE`, `PNG_RESTRICT`, `PNG_UNUSED(x)` are no-ops.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     78[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `PNG_NORETURN` means the Rust fn returns `!`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     79[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `png_voidcast(t,v)`, `png_constcast(t,v)`, `png_aligncast(t,v)`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     80[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `png_aligncastconst(t,v)` are plain casts.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     81[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `png_debug*(...)` calls translate to **nothing** (delete them).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     82[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     83[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `PNG_FUNCTION(type, name, args, attrs)` is just a function definition:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     84[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `PNG_FUNCTION(void,PNGAPI png_error,(png_const_structrp p, png_const_charp m),
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     85[0m:[38;5;10m[49m PNG_NORETURN)` == `void png_error(png_const_structrp p, png_const_charp m)`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     86[0m:[38;5;10m[49m that never returns.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     87[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     88[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ---
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     89[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     90[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## 2. Mandatory Rust conventions
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     91[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     92[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Every translated file starts with:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     93[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     94[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```rust
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     95[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! Translation of c_src/src/<FILE>.c lines <A>..<B>
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     96[0m:[38;5;10m[49m use crate::prelude::*;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     97[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     98[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     99[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### 2.1 Function signatures
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    100[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    101[0m:[38;5;10m[49m *Every* C function in your range becomes:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    102[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    103[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```rust
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    104[0m:[38;5;10m[49m pub unsafe extern "C" fn <exact_c_name>(<args>) -> <ret> { ... }
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    105[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    106[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    107[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * Keep the **exact C name** (also for C `static` functions).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    108[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * Mark it `pub` **even if it was `static` in C** (other chunks of the same C
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    109[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   file live in sibling Rust modules and reach it through the prelude).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    110[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * If the name appears in `/tmp/pngwork.3SUdKO/exported_symbols.txt`, it is part
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    111[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   of the public ABI and **must** additionally carry `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]`:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    112[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    113[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```rust
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    114[0m:[38;5;10m[49m #[unsafe(no_mangle)]
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    115[0m:[38;5;10m[49m pub unsafe extern "C" fn png_set_sig_bytes(png_ptr: png_structrp, num_bytes: c_int) { ... }
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    116[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    117[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    118[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   Check with:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    119[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `grep -x 'png_foo' /tmp/pngwork.3SUdKO/exported_symbols.txt`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    120[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   Do **not** put `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]` on anything that is not in that list.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    121[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * C `PNG_NORETURN` functions (`png_error`, `png_chunk_error`, `png_longjmp`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    122[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `png_fixed_error`, `png_safe_error`) return `!` in Rust.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    123[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * Parameter/return types come from `types.rs`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    124[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (`png_structrp`, `png_const_structrp`, `png_bytep`, `png_uint_32`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    125[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `png_alloc_size_t`, `c_int`, `usize`, ...).  `int` -> `c_int`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    126[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `unsigned int` -> `c_uint`, `size_t` -> `usize`, `double` -> `f64`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    127[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `char*` -> `png_charp`/`*mut c_char`, `void*` -> `png_voidp`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    128[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    129[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### 2.2 Statics / global data
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    130[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    131[0m:[38;5;10m[49m C file-scope `static const` tables become
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    132[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    133[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```rust
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    134[0m:[38;5;10m[49m static NAME: [T; N] = [ ... ];
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    135[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    136[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    137[0m:[38;5;10m[49m C non-const file-scope statics become `static mut` (access inside `unsafe`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    138[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The three *exported* data arrays (`png_sRGB_table`, `png_sRGB_base`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    139[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `png_sRGB_delta`) must be
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    140[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    141[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```rust
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    142[0m:[38;5;10m[49m #[unsafe(no_mangle)]
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    143[0m:[38;5;10m[49m pub static png_sRGB_base: [png_uint_16; 512] = [ ... ];
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    144[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    145[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    146[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (and must keep every element value exactly).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    147[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    148[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### 2.3 C semantics that MUST be preserved
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    149[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    150[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 1. **Integer promotion.**  In C every operand narrower than `int` is promoted to
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    151[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `int` *before* the operation.  Rust does not do this.  Always insert the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    152[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    casts:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    153[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    ```c
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    154[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    png_byte a, b; int d = a - b;          /* may be negative */
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    155[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    156[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    ```rust
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    157[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    let d: c_int = a as c_int - b as c_int; // NOT (a - b) as c_int
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    158[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    159[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    The same applies to `png_uint_16 * png_uint_16` (C: int arithmetic, may
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    160[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    overflow to negative), `<<` on `png_byte`, comparisons, etc.  Getting this
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    161[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    wrong silently corrupts output — be meticulous.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    162[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 2. **Wrap-around.**  The release profile disables overflow checks, but write
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    163[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `wrapping_add` / `wrapping_sub` / `wrapping_mul` wherever the C code relies
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    164[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    on modular arithmetic (CRC, hashes, `-1` sentinels, `0U - x`, ...).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    165[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 3. **Truncating casts.**  `(png_byte)x` -> `x as png_byte`, `(int)x` ->
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    166[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `x as c_int`; `as` truncates exactly like C.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    167[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 4. **Float -> int** casts in C truncate toward zero; `as` does the same
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    168[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    (Rust saturates on out-of-range instead of UB — keep the C expression shape,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    169[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    do not add clamping of your own).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    170[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 5. **Order of evaluation / short circuit** of `&&`, `||` must be preserved,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    171[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    including any side effects.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    172[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 6. **Do not fix bugs.**  If the C looks wrong, translate it wrong.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    173[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 7. **Do not reorder** validation or error checks.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    174[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 8. `sizeof(x)` -> `core::mem::size_of::<T>()`;
