[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    176[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    matches the C layout.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    177[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    178[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### 2.4 Pointers
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    179[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    180[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `p->field` -> `(*p).field`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    181[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `p + n` -> `p.add(n as usize)` (or `.offset(n as isize)` when `n` can be
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    182[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   negative); `p - n` -> `p.sub(n as usize)`; `p1 - p2` ->
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    183[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `p1.offset_from(p2)`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    184[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `*p++ = v` -> `*p = v; p = p.add(1);`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    185[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `NULL` -> `core::ptr::null_mut()` / `core::ptr::null()`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    186[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `(void)x;` -> delete.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    187[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * Casting between pointer types: `p as *mut T`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    188[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * Struct-valued assignment `*a = *b;` -> `*a = *b;` works for `Copy` structs
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    189[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   in `types.rs`; use `core::ptr::write`/`read` if not `Copy`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    190[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    191[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### 2.5 Function pointers in structs
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    192[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    193[0m:[38;5;10m[49m They are `Option<unsafe extern "C" fn(..)>` in `types.rs`:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    194[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
